From: Riley <oreo4455@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fixed orientation for apps that pin one, while the shell rotates

X-Phosh-Orientation=landscape in an app's desktop file pins its view to landscape
while fullscreen: it keeps the landscape size (and gets it as its configure bounds,
or GTK keeps it within the monitor's size) and is drawn in that orientation
whatever the output's transform, with damage and input mapped through it, while
the output (and so Phosh's panels, home bar and shade) rotates with the device: a
camera app held either way. No modeset shield over it (it doesn't move): the
shell's top layer waits instead, until a rotation's new layout is in. Direct
scanout compares the buffer's transform with the view's, so a client that
pre-rotates its buffers to it is still scanned out.
